## 🎯 Day 35 Objective

Yesterday's Risk Register (Day 34) needs a *front door*. That front door is the **AI Intake & Impact Assessment (AIA)** — the form every new AI use case fills out *before* it gets built or bought. It's where governance shifts left: you catch a high-risk, EU-AI-Act-regulated, PII-hungry use case at the idea stage, not after it's in production.

Today I built a **two-stage AIA**: a lightweight **Intake Triage** (5 minutes, anyone can fill it) that routes a use case to the right level of review, followed by a **Full Impact Assessment** (only for use cases the triage flags). This is directly modeled on **ISO 42001 Clause 6.1.2** (AI system impact assessment) and the **EU AI Act** high-risk classification logic.

