## 🚦 The Tiering Model

Not every use case deserves a 20-page assessment. The triage sorts use cases into three tiers and routes accordingly:

| Tier | Description | Review Required | Example |
|------|-------------|-----------------|---------|
| **Tier 3 — Minimal** | Internal productivity, no personal data, no consequential decisions | Self-attest + register entry | Summarizing public docs |
| **Tier 2 — Limited** | Some personal data OR affects internal users, reversible decisions | Lightweight review by AI gov lead | Internal knowledge chatbot |
| **Tier 1 — High** | Consequential decisions about people, sensitive data, or an EU-AI-Act Annex III domain | **Full Impact Assessment + governance board** | Hiring, credit, healthcare, biometric use cases |

**Auto-escalation triggers** — any *one* of these forces Tier 1 regardless of triage answers:
- The system makes or materially influences a decision about a person's **employment, credit, housing, education, healthcare, insurance, or legal status**
- It processes **special-category data** (health, biometrics, race, religion, sexual orientation, criminal history)
- It's a use case named in **EU AI Act Annex III** (high-risk) or **Article 5** (prohibited — auto-reject)
- It affects **children** or other vulnerable groups
- It operates with **no meaningful human review** of its outputs

