## 📝 Part B — Full Impact Assessment (Tier 1)

### Section 1 — Purpose & Context
- Intended purpose and explicitly **out-of-scope** uses
- Business value and the cost of *not* doing it
- Who decided to build this and why now

### Section 2 — Data
- Data sources (training, fine-tuning, inference/retrieval) with provenance and licensing
- Personal / special-category data used, legal basis, and consent status
- Data minimization: what's collected vs. what's actually needed
- Retention, deletion, and cross-border transfer

### Section 3 — The Model / System
- Model type, vendor/version, and whether it's foundation-model-based
- Known limitations, accuracy expectations, and evaluation approach
- Whether inputs are used to train the vendor's model (for third-party)

### Section 4 — Affected People & Rights Impact
- Who is affected (users, subjects of decisions, third parties, non-users)
- **Rights & harms analysis:** could this affect dignity, non-discrimination, privacy, access to services, safety, or autonomy?
- Disproportionate impact on any group; fairness testing plan
- Worst realistic case for an individual on the receiving end of a wrong output

### Section 5 — Human Oversight
- Where a human is in / on / out of the loop
- What the human can actually do (override, escalate, halt) and whether they have the info/time to do it
- Guard against **automation bias** (people rubber-stamping the AI)

### Section 6 — Alternatives & Proportionality
- Non-AI or simpler alternatives considered
- Why the chosen approach is proportionate to the problem
- Whether the least-intrusive option was selected

### Section 7 — Risk Summary & Treatment
- Top 5 risks → feed straight into the **Day 34 Risk Register**
- Residual risk after planned controls
- Monitoring plan and re-assessment triggers

