## ✅ The Decision Gate

The AIA ends in one of four outcomes, recorded with a named decision-maker and date:

| Outcome | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| 🟢 **Approved** | Proceed; register the system and its risks |
| 🟡 **Approved with conditions** | Proceed only after listed controls are in place; conditions tracked to closure |
| 🟠 **Escalate** | Governance board / DPO / legal decision required before proceeding |
| 🔴 **Rejected** | Do not proceed (prohibited use, disproportionate risk, or unmitigable harm) |

> **Non-negotiable:** no Tier 1 AI system goes to production without a completed AIA and a recorded decision. The AIA is the evidence an ISO 42001 auditor or EU AI Act regulator will ask for first.

